  "result": "I couldn't get a real gate verdict. Both runs I made returned `SCOPE_VIOLATION`, and the cause was this session's tooling, not the concept files. The shell tool writes a temporary output file for each command (`.runtime/tmp/…/tasks/<id>.output`), and the gate counts it as a change outside the concept's files. Each run flagged the file for that run only, so every run from this shell would fail the same way. I stopped after 2 of the 6 runs. The harness's own gate run after this session doesn't go through that shell, so its verdict is the one that counts.\n\nOne other thing was blocked: a `grep` over Core, because the shell is limited to the gate command. I read `Core/Language/Semantics.lean` with the Read tool instead. It confirmed that position, velocity and the region's reference point are read one component at a time, with `x`/`y` selectors.\n\n**Concept** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/circulating_clockwise_about.lean`)\n- With d = a's position − r's reference point and v = a's velocity, the body requires all three of:\n  - `dx·vy < dy·vx`, which is the contract's \"cross product of d with a's velocity is negative\", written without a literal zero;\n  - `(dx·vy − dy·vx)² > sin_tol²·(dx²+dy²)·speed²`;\n  - `kin_speed a > speed_tol`.\n- It uses exactly the four claimed atoms and no division. I declared no narrowings, because the contract states the inequalities exactly.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/circulating_clockwise_about.lean`)\n- The instance sets `speed_tol` = 1 m/s and `sin_tol` = 1/2.\n- A car circles the roundabout's reference point at the origin at 5 m/s, 10 m away, over three instants.\n- **holds:** it goes clockwise, so the cross product is −50 at each instant.\n- **fails:** it goes counter-clockwise, so the cross product is +50.\n- **blind:** the same clockwise motion, with the region mapped without a reference point or boundary and `st.region_geometry` declared absent.\n\n**Possible `VACUOUS` verdict:** `fails` only tests the direction, as its narrative says. No scenario makes the turn-share condition or the `speed_tol` condition the one that fails. If the harness's check needs that, the fix is a `fails` instant where the car moves almost straight towards or away from the point, or below `speed_tol`.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory records both runs, these choices and why I stopped.",
